  "subject": "A Central observation-wheel operator who holds the wheel still for three extra seconds at the top for an old woman who rides alone every Tuesday to look at the old Star Ferry pier where she once worked as a typist, and who one Tuesday asks the operator why he never rides himself.",
  "caption": "Cantonese Cuban danzon, elegant 2/4 promenade. A wooden flute playing the lead melody, a string section of violins with elegant portamento, a grand piano with a lilting cinquillo pattern, timbales and guiro keeping a steady 2/4 danzon pulse, upright bass. Warm 1950s ballroom orchestra recording, soft room reverb, rounded vintage tone. Male tenor, smooth and courtly, light vibrato, clearly sung melody on every line. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 92 BPM, F major. Courtly, nostalgic, gentle. No trap drums, no autotune, no rap, no electric guitar, no synth pads, no fast salsa section.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n中環海旁 我管住摩天輪\n每個禮拜二 午後三點半\n有個老婆婆 一個人排隊\n手袋夾住 一張舊相\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n圈圈慢慢轉 轉到最高\n我㩒住掣 多停三秒\n\n[Chorus]\n多停三秒 多停三秒\n等你睇清楚 嗰個碼頭\n多停三秒 唔使人知\n整個城市 靜落嚟\n\n[Verse]\n佢話 當年喺嗰度做打字員\n每朝趕渡輪 裙腳飄起\n而家碼頭拆咗 剩返片海\n佢睇住片海 輕輕笑\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n後面排隊嘅遊客\n有人催 有人望錶\n\n[Chorus]\n多停三秒 多停三秒\n等你睇清楚 嗰個碼頭\n多停三秒 唔使人知\n我當冇聽到 啲人催\n\n[Verse]\n有個禮拜二 佢落嚟時問我\n你日日喺度 點解自己唔坐\n我笑一笑 唔知點答\n佢拉住我手 話 上嚟\n\n[Bridge]\n我第一次 坐上自己部機\n佢喺下面 幫我㩒掣\n停喺最高 三秒\n\n[Chorus]\n多停三秒 多停三秒\n原來嗰個碼頭 咁近\n多停三秒 唔使人知\n下個禮拜二 我都喺度\n\n[Outro]\n多停三秒\n慢慢轉",
